<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aljustrel</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Aljustrel is a town in the Beja district of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alentejo">Alentejo</a> in southern Portugal, in the Iberian Pyrite Belt. Its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/copper">copper</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> deposits were worked in Roman times at the mining district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vipasca">Vipasca</a>, where bronze tablets preserving imperial mining regulations were found in 1876 and 1906. Mining has continued into modern times, and the town remains a centre of the Portuguese mining industry.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/aljustrel.jpg" alt="Aljustrel" width="320" height="134" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Claus Bunk · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aljustrel.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
